.TH ORG 1 "August 2026" "org (organise)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
org \- Automatically sort and move files into designated directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B org
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B org
is a fast, C++ based command-line tool that automatically organizes files in a directory based on predefined rules. It supports regex matching, extension grouping, continuous watching (recursively) using inotify, and activity logging.
.P
Configuration is read from
.I ~/.config/organise/config.json
(see
.BR \-\-config ).
All file moves are logged with timestamps to
.I ~/.local/state/organise/activity.log
, which is especially useful in watch mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Simulate actions without actually moving files.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Scan directories recursively (process all subdirectories).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Display detailed execution output.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-auto\-rename
Automatically rename conflicting files without prompting the user.
.TP
.BR \-\-conflict=\fIMODE\fR
Set conflict strategy. Valid modes are: \fIrename\fR, \fIskip\fR, or \fIoverwrite\fR.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch
Watch the directory and all subdirectories continuously, organising new files as they appear (recursively).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config=\fIFILE\fR
Use a specific configuration file instead of the default path.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-undo
Undo the last batch of moves, using the history log.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display the project's version and exit.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/organise/config.json
.RS
Default configuration file (JSON format). If it does not exist, it is automatically created with example rules.
.RE
.I ~/.local/state/organise/history.json
.RS
History of moves used for undo operations.
.RE
.I ~/.local/state/organise/activity.log
.RS
Activity log with timestamps for all moves and errors.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Organize files in the current directory with verbose output:
.RS
.B org -v .
.RE
Simulate what would happen in a recursive scan:
.RS
.B org -n -r ~/Downloads
.RE
Watch a directory continuously:
.RS
.B org --watch ~/Downloads
.RE
Undo the last operation:
.RS
.B org -u
.RE
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/rafael-hacker/organise/issues
